<BaseLayout title="AI Systems Reliability Lab — Model Regression Gate" description="A bounded AI reliability experiment comparing two frozen configurations across 30 synthetic cases, with deterministic release checks and a post-experiment audit of the semantic evaluator itself.">
  <article class="lab-case-study">
    <header class="lab-hero shell">
      <p class="eyebrow">Focused technical proof · Lab 01</p>
      <h1>Frozen AI regression gate<br />with evaluator validation</h1>
      <p class="lab-subtitle">A bounded AI reliability experiment comparing two frozen configurations across 30 synthetic cases, with deterministic release checks and a post-experiment audit of the semantic evaluator itself.</p>
      <p class="lab-summary">Built a frozen AI regression gate to test whether a proposed configuration was safe to release. Both configurations passed deterministic checks, but the automated semantic quality gate failed the candidate. A human audit of all 60 outputs then found the local semantic judge unreliable as release authority while confirming the candidate had materially lower factual support than the baseline.</p>
      <p class="lab-cta"><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/ai-systems-reliability-lab">View the evidence on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></p>
    </header>

    <section class="lab-ledger shell" aria-label="Experiment evidence at a glance">
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Frozen experiment</p><strong>30 cases</strong><span>Synthetic support-triage workflow</span></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Deterministic validation</p><strong>30 / 30</strong><span>Both configurations · 0 regressions</span></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Automated release gate</p><strong>FAIL</strong><span>58.6% factual support vs 90% threshold</span></article>
      <article><p class="eyebrow">Human audit</p><strong>60 / 60</strong><span>Generated outputs reviewed</span></article>
    </section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-problem"><div class="lab-label"><p class="eyebrow">01 · Problem</p></div><div class="lab-body"><h2 id="lab-problem">Can a proposed AI configuration be evaluated before release?</h2><p>The experiment separates mechanical validity from semantic quality. A configuration can satisfy a schema and deterministic rules while still producing answers that need stronger factual support.</p></div></section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-method"><div class="lab-label"><p class="eyebrow">02 · Frozen experiment</p></div><div class="lab-body"><h2 id="lab-method">The decision logic was fixed before the golden execution.</h2><p>The dataset, prompts, model configuration, schema, evaluators, thresholds, and release logic were frozen before final execution. A contaminated execution was preserved as aborted rather than normalized into a convenient result.</p><div class="lab-method-grid"><div><strong>Decision hypothesis</strong><span>Do not release a candidate configuration if it regresses against the frozen quality threshold.</span></div><div><strong>Deterministic checks</strong><span>Baseline 30 / 30 · Candidate 30 / 30 · 0 hard-gate violations.</span></div><div><strong>Semantic release gate</strong><span>Candidate factual-support score: 58.6%, below the frozen 90% threshold.</span></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-decision"><div class="lab-label"><p class="eyebrow">03 · Historical decision</p></div><div class="lab-body"><h2 id="lab-decision">The automated FAIL remained part of the record.</h2><ol class="lab-decision-chain"><li><strong>Deterministic checks</strong><span>PASS for both frozen configurations.</span></li><li><strong>Semantic release gate</strong><span>FAIL: the candidate remained below the 90% factual-support threshold.</span></li><li><strong>Human audit</strong><span>The evaluator’s release authority was challenged after review of all 60 outputs.</span></li><li><strong>Historical record</strong><span>The original automated FAIL was preserved; later evidence added interpretation, not a rewrite.</span></li></ol></div></section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-audit"><div class="lab-label"><p class="eyebrow">04 · Post-experiment audit</p></div><div class="lab-body"><h2 id="lab-audit">The evaluator was tested rather than trusted by default.</h2><p class="lab-finding">The local semantic evaluator was not reliable enough to serve as release authority in this bounded experiment.</p><p>Human review independently confirmed that the candidate had materially lower factual support than the baseline. The evaluator’s weakness did not make the candidate safe.</p><table class="lab-comparison"><caption>Human audit comparison</caption><thead><tr><th scope="col">Measure</th><th scope="col">Baseline</th><th scope="col">Candidate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><th scope="row">Human-confirmed factual support</th><td>96.7%</td><td>70.0%</td></tr><tr><th scope="row">Judge / human agreement</th><td>53.3%</td><td>43.3%</td></tr></tbody></table><p class="lab-note">A release gate is only as trustworthy as the evaluator it delegates judgment to. In this bounded experiment, human review showed the local semantic evaluator had not earned that authority.</p></div></section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-role"><div class="lab-label"><p class="eyebrow">05 · System judgment</p></div><div class="lab-body"><h2 id="lab-role">Make the evidence visible. Keep authority explicit.</h2><div class="lab-authorship"><div><strong>Evidence integrity</strong><span>Contaminated evidence was rejected rather than made convenient.</span></div><div><strong>Frozen variables</strong><span>The final comparison did not move its own goalposts.</span></div><div><strong>Evaluator skepticism</strong><span>A scoring component was audited before being granted release authority.</span></div><div><strong>Human oversight</strong><span>Human review added interpretation without erasing history.</span></div></div></div></section>

    <section class="lab-section shell" aria-labelledby="lab-boundary"><div class="lab-label"><p class="eyebrow">06 · Current boundary</p></div><div class="lab-body"><h2 id="lab-boundary">A small, inspectable experiment—not a general claim.</h2><div class="lab-boundaries"><div><p class="eyebrow">What it demonstrates</p><ul><li>Frozen experiment discipline</li><li>Deterministic validation and release gating</li><li>Evaluator validation and human oversight</li></ul></div><div><p class="eyebrow">What it does not claim</p><ul><li>A production benchmark or autonomous release system</li><li>A general finding about all LLM-as-judge systems</li><li>Production reliability or observability platform capability</li></ul></div></div><p class="lab-note">Synthetic local experiment. $0 API/service spend.</p></div></section>

    <section class="lab-evidence shell" aria-labelledby="lab-evidence"><p class="eyebrow">07 · Inspect the evidence</p><h2 id="lab-evidence">The public record is one click away.</h2><p>Explore the reviewed evidence set, decision record, and semantic-audit report in the public repository.</p><a class="text-link" href="https://github.com/matt-rfs/ai-systems-reliability-lab">View the evidence on GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
